# autotest alpha.10, lane B1 (2026-11-24): the UI as its own program on a booted image. Written against the Feature text with sha cdfe282a641b4e83; honest subset only: everything not checked is under not-covered.
row: F-SPLIT-03
targets: qemu
profile: ui_process
feature-sha: cdfe282a641b4e83
doc: with iyakki.ui=process the core runs the shell as the program iyakki-ui, its child, over the core's socket
clause: 1 the program iyakki-ui (shell and apps) is supervised by the core: process 1 is the core, iyakki-ui its child with the socket argument, the core has no shell thread, the boot screen lets go of the display
not-covered: real hardware (a real display, a touch screen, a GPU), the tiles that need a live object of the core (FLOWS, TALES, LAB, STORE, RADIO, MEDIA: they say so in the program), the apps-only push of a ui layer to a device
session-check: ui_process_tree
